depression and anxiety. Now here's one that really startled me. High levels of rule breaking. Now we're talking about random acts of delinquency. We found levels are comparable actually to levels in inner city settings. The only difference is the inner city kids are doing things like carrying a gun or getting into a fight and so on, which could potentially be in self-protection and gangs. Our upper middle class kids are doing things like stealing from a friend or stealing from a parent or defacing property, as I said, random acts of delinquency. And these rates are much higher, again, two to two and a half times as high as average rates in America. Then there is envy, particularly among our girls, levels of envy of peers are much higher than we find among inner-city girls or boys
抑郁和焦虑。现在有一个让我非常震惊的问题。高水平的违规行为。我们谈论的是随机的犯罪行为。我们发现其水平实际上与内城环境中的水平相当。唯一的区别是，内城区的孩子做的事情比如携带枪支或打架等等，这可能出于自我保护和帮派原因。我们的中上层阶级孩子做的事情比如从朋友那里偷东西，或者从父母那里偷东西，或者破坏财产，正如我所说，是随机的犯罪行为。这些比率要高得多，同样是美国平均水平的2到2.5倍。然后是嫉妒，特别是在我们的女孩中，对同龄人的嫉妒程度远高于我们在内城区女孩或男孩中发现的水平，

